LANGFUSE TROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE #1
=================================

ISSUE
-----
Langfuse container exits immediately after startup.

Command Used:

docker run -d --name langfuse -p 3000:3000 langfuse/langfuse


SYMPTOM
-------
Check containers:

docker ps -a

Output:

STATUS
Exited (1)


ROOT CAUSE
----------
Check logs:

docker logs langfuse

Error:

Required database environment variables are not set.
Provide a postgres url for DATABASE_URL.

Explanation:

Langfuse cannot run without PostgreSQL.
A DATABASE_URL environment variable must be supplied.


STEP 1 - START POSTGRESQL
-------------------------

Create PostgreSQL container:

docker run -d --name postgres -e POSTGRES_USER=langfuse -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=langfuse123 -e POSTGRES_DB=langfuse -p 5432:5432 postgres:16

Verify:

docker ps

Expected:

postgres   Up


STEP 2 - REMOVE FAILED LANGFUSE CONTAINER
-----------------------------------------

docker rm -f langfuse


STEP 3 - CREATE DOCKER NETWORK
------------------------------

docker network create langfuse-net

Purpose:
Allow Langfuse and PostgreSQL containers to communicate.


STEP 4 - START POSTGRESQL IN NETWORK
------------------------------------

docker run -d --name postgres --network langfuse-net -e POSTGRES_USER=langfuse -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=langfuse123 -e POSTGRES_DB=langfuse postgres:16


STEP 5 - START LANGFUSE
-----------------------

docker run -d --name langfuse --network langfuse-net -p 3000:3000 -e DATABASE_URL="postgresql://langfuse:langfuse123@postgres:5432/langfuse" langfuse/langfuse


